lodge_exact_incipit:
And the potentates of Ierusalem, and Ananus 
                         the high Priest, with all speed renued and repaired the wals, and made all sorts of instruments

for warre,

And any

death were easie in respect of famine. So that many fled vnto the Romans, hauing no promise,  
                         no nor hope to be pardoned by them, and vpon purpose fell into the hands of the seditious;
